  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With the EAC causing a massive uproar, I wanted to throw a suggestion into the mix. Create a separate client which allows mods and can be easily identified when reporting a bug. Then also make it so when loading from a mod list, this would be a list of keys that gets and injects the mods from a webservice as to curate what is and isnt allowed. Then have those who use it understand ifs not vrcs responsibility to ensure the stability of the modded client (as mods can break things in updates). This will normalize the use of mods through an official client to ensure safe use of mods, and we can either curate them through the community or if you want to set aside something like a code review when mods are released or updated. I think everyone can agree there are good mods and we want to stop the use of bad mods, and there is still a lot more that will need to be done to ensure security, but figured dedicating mods to a different client might be a start.",
